1
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,599
If you can deal with her,

2
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:54,159
name your price. Money is no object.

3
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:58,639
With that kind of money,
that Sarai ghost will be gone soon.

4
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:01,919
Pakarang's body can only remain preserved

5
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,279
<i>through blood.</i>

6
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,679
Blood?

7
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:07,079
<i>Thon, I love you more than anything.</i>

8
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:10,399
So can you tell me now?
Who exactly is Pakarang?

9
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:12,800
Ms. Sarai, are you here?

10
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:28,719
When Narathon called
and said he was coming,

11
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:32,720
I didn't expect
all of you to arrive so soon.

12
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:38,960
We happened to have
some business in this area.

13
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:44,559
We were already planning
to come and pay our respects.

14
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:48,680
May I ask what you wanted to see me about?

15
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:52,400
I will be going
on a pilgrimage for some time.

16
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:56,320
I'm worried about Kang.

17
00:03:56,960 --> 00:04:01,440
There will be no one to look after him,
so I'd like to ask you

18
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:06,360
to take care of him for me.
Would that be inconvenient?

19
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:11,320
Not at all. I'd be happy to.

20
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:14,200
Thank you.

21
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:20,160
Just think of Kang as a younger brother.

22
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,679
During his stay,

23
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:27,760
I'll take care of him
as if he was my own brother.

24
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:35,320
Kang, when you stay with Narathon,

25
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:38,040
obey him.

26
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:40,720
Even if he scolds you from time to time,

27
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:44,599
think of it as an older brother
teaching his younger brother.

28
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:46,639
Yes, Venerable Sir.

29
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:48,479
Remember this.

30
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:50,919
No matter where you go,

31
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:53,599
there is one thing
you must always keep and practice,

32
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:57,040
just as you have done here at this temple.

33
00:04:58,160 --> 00:05:01,360
Do good things.

34
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:06,320
Goodness will be your shield.

35
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:12,000
It will protect you from danger
throughout your life.

36
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:17,880
You're making it sound as though
you'll be gone for a very long time.

37
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:23,040
Nothing in life is certain.
We may be speaking together today,

38
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:28,520
but tomorrow we may never meet again
for the rest of our lives.

39
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:39,760
Can't I go with you, Venerable Sir?
I can look after you.

40
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,840
No, Kang.

41
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:45,640
The place I'm going to
is not suitable for you.

42
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:49,680
Alright.

43
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,840
Now hurry along.

44
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:56,240
You'll want to reach Bangkok before dark.

45
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:05,600
I'm leaving now, Venerable Sir.
Please take good care of yourself.

46
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:07,720
You too.

47
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:13,960
Let's go.

48
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:35,880
Here.

49
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:42,960
Shall we go now?

50
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:46,759
Go find something to eat and relax first.

51
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:48,920
Come back and pick me up tonight.

52
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:53,560
Why tonight? You've already got the money.

53
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:59,080
I need time to prepare the necessary items
for dealing with the spirit.

54
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:01,120
More importantly,

55
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:04,400
there is an auspicious time
for the journey.

56
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:10,559
Tonight's hour is favorable
and will ensure success.

57
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:15,320
We must leave at nine minutes past nine.

58
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:19,960
- So about 9 p.m. tonight.
- 9 p.m.?

59
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:22,320
That's right.

60
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,800
Do we really have to wait that long?

61
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:30,639
If you don't trust me,
take your money back.

62
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:32,720
I'm not interested
in such a small amount anyway.

63
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:40,280
Alright. Then I'll come back for you
at nine tonight.

64
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:43,760
That's more like it.

65
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,280
Here.

66
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:00,520
Oh?

67
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:06,000
- It's closed?
- Oh?

68
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:09,160
Is this the only
boat service there is, Prawin?

69
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:11,679
There are several others,

70
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:14,960
but none of them are willing to go
to Skull Island. This is the only one.

71
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,639
Are you going to Skull Island?

72
00:09:31,640 --> 00:09:33,920
- Nope.
- Oh.

73
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:37,400
Come on.

74
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,320
How'd it go, Win?

75
00:09:42,680 --> 00:09:44,200
He won't go.

76
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:46,680
He won't?

77
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:49,600
Why is it that no matter who we ask,
nobody wants to go?

78
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:54,720
Or are they just trying
to jack up the price?

79
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,560
What are they all so scared of?

80
00:09:58,200 --> 00:09:59,320
Exactly.

81
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:07,160
- Hey, Win. Look over there.
- Huh?

82
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:13,560
Come on, Pat. That boat's not an option.
It's not a charter boat.

83
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,760
A boat's a boat, isn't it?

84
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,439
I've come all this way.

85
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:23,000
- There's no way I'm leaving empty-handed.
- Pat.

86
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:25,360
What are you planning to do?

87
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:28,400
Just stay quiet. I'll handle this.

88
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:32,320
Pat. Pat.

89
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,040
Can I help you?

90
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,840
Um...

91
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,640
Is this your boat?

92
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:57,440
No. It belongs to my boss.
Is there something you need?

93
00:10:58,280 --> 00:11:02,680
We have some business on the island
and were hoping to catch a ride.

94
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:06,280
This isn't a passenger boat.

95
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:11,440
But we really do need to get there.
Just name your price.

96
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,200
Like I said, this isn't a passenger boat.

97
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:27,320
Where exactly are you trying to go?

98
00:11:28,160 --> 00:11:30,959
We're trying to get to Skull Island,

99
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:34,600
but no matter how many boats we ask,
none of them will take us.

100
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:40,599
Looks like fate is on our side.
I'm heading there myself.

101
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:45,079
If you don't mind,
you're welcome to travel with me.

102
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:47,599
That would be an honor.

103
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:51,080
Oh, I forgot to introduce myself. I'm Pat.

104
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:56,280
I'm Men.

105
00:11:58,160 --> 00:12:00,839
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you too.

106
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:05,440
I thought your man said
you don't take passengers.

107
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:14,360
My apologies. My man
isn't very good at understanding things.

108
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:19,520
I told you to keep quiet.
Don't say a word.

109
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:25,640
It's alright. My companion isn't very good
at understanding things either.

110
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:41,999
Well,

111
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,920
Thon, why are we here? Are you sick?

112
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:51,840
I forgot to tell you.
Your Mr. Phum is in the hospital.

113
00:12:52,680 --> 00:12:55,240
Is it serious?

114
00:12:57,520 --> 00:13:00,039
Looks like
you're really worried about him.

115
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:02,160
I am. Mr. Phum is very kind.

116
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:08,240
- Then shall we go visit him now?
- Yes.

117
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:14,880
- Hello.
- Hello.

118
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:21,160
Poor kid. You're still so young, yet
you've had to move from place to place.

119
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:24,440
Except Venerable Sir,

120
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:26,640
Kang has no one left.

121
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:30,999
Why don't you come stay with us
while the Venerable Sir is away.

122
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,200
Thon and I will take care of you.

123
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:39,000
Thank you. I'll do whatever I can to help.
I'm not lazy, I promise.

124
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:42,279
Listen to that.
Giving yourself a sales pitch already.

125
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:45,039
I can stay here
and keep you company tonight.

126
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:47,640
I've stayed overnight at hospitals
with Venerable Sir before.

127
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:51,759
Perfect. I was just
looking for someone to talk to.

128
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:53,479
Then you'll stay here with me tonight.

129
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:55,999
- Yes.
- But...

130
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:59,119
It's fine. Pakarang is here too.
She can help look after things.

131
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:02,040
But Pakarang isn't feeling well.

132
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:04,000
Pakarang's all better now.

133
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:09,600
Does that mean
she finally agreed to the blood test?

134
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:14,119
It's a long story.
Let's talk about it after we get home.

135
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:17,160
You should go get some rest.

136
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:22,679
Come on, Kang.
Let me see what you have in your bag.

137
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:24,080
Sure.

138
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:27,800
Wow, you even have a sacred yantra shirt?

139
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:30,919
So knives can't pierce it, right?

140
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:32,999
- No.
- Try it on. I'll test it with a knife.

141
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:33,919
Alright?

142
00:14:33,920 --> 00:14:36,999
In that case, I'd better get going.

143
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,400
Drive safely, son.

144
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:43,880
- That's a pretty big shirt. Will it fit?
- Yes.

145
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:50,639
Alright then. You've had a long ride.
Go take a shower, then we can talk.

146
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:51,880
Alright.

147
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:03,560
Mr. Narathon.

148
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:09,519
Ms. Pakarang, you're feeling better now?

149
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:10,840
Yes.

150
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:15,120
So what exactly is your condition?

151
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,519
I asked Dad, but he wouldn't tell me.

152
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:20,000
Oh.

153
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:23,160
It's a condition...

154
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:26,800
related to a woman's internal system.
Blood circulation and things like that.

155
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,280
I see.

156
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:34,119
See? I told you
that you wouldn't understand.

157
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:38,600
Let's just say I'm fine now. Don't worry.

158
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:42,320
Are you here to visit Mr. Phum?

159
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:44,199
Yes.

160
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:48,559
Then let's go up together.
I came down to buy a coffee for him.

161
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:51,560
He was craving one,
but he's afraid the doctor will scold him.

162
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:57,000
I'm actually heading home.
I brought Kang to visit him,

163
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:01,120
but Kang asked to stay here
with him tonight.

164
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:03,200
Kang?

165
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:08,280
Kang is the temple boy
who looks after my fish pond.

166
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:10,200
Oh, is that so?

167
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:14,560
Then I'd better get him
some cocoa and cake too.

168
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:20,560
Thank you. Please take care
of Dad and Kang for me.

169
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:23,680
Of course. Don't worry.

170
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:36,240
Hello.

171
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:45,000
Kang,
why are you looking at her like that?

172
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:53,560
I bet you're thinking
I'm pretty, aren't you?

173
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:55,839
Yes.

174
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,639
You're very pretty, ma'am.

175
00:16:57,640 --> 00:16:59,319
Oh.

176
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:03,400
Smooth talker already?
You're something else.

177
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,039
You're such a sweet boy. Come here.

178
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:09,880
We just met for the first time
and I already like you.

179
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:24,318
You're so sweet.

180
00:17:24,319 --> 00:17:28,159
Come have some cake. I bought it for you.

181
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:31,240
- Yes.
- How did you know Kang was here?

182
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:34,000
I ran into Mr. Narathon downstairs.

183
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:49,040
Looks like this little guy
has stolen my personal nurse.

184
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:53,600
Here you are. I'll feed you too.

185
00:17:57,520 --> 00:18:00,079
Otherwise, you'll accuse me
of neglecting my duties.

186
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:02,839
That's more like it.

187
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:04,399
- Is it delicious, Kang?
- It is.

188
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:06,080
- Then eat more.
- Have one more bite.

189
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:12,440
- You like the cheese, right?
- Yes.

190
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:20,760
Master Kong.

191
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,400
Master Kong, are you there?

192
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:30,880
Master Kong.

193
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:37,080
Don't tell me
the master packed up and ran away.

194
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,559
What nonsense are you talking about?
Go call him.

195
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:43,520
Maybe he's fallen asleep
while waiting for us.

196
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,000
Master Kong.

197
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:57,800
Master Kong.

198
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:00,000
Master Kong, are you here?

199
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:24,400
This is the spirit child's topknot.

200
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:36,559
We've been conned.

201
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:39,639
That means they fooled us?

202
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:40,800
Of course.

203
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:44,520
Damn it!

204
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:50,120
Ugh.

205
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,520
The food looks delicious.

206
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:07,200
A lot of them are my favorites.

207
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:10,320
Looks like
we have the same taste yet again.

208
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:14,360
Thank you.

209
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:18,360
Thank you.

210
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:35,880
Please enjoy.

211
00:20:50,640 --> 00:20:51,560
Whoa.

212
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:56,159
Isn't this beef a little too rare?
There's still so much blood.

213
00:20:56,160 --> 00:20:58,559
- I can't eat that.
- Win,

214
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:02,839
don't be so fussy.
That's what makes it delicious.

215
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:04,680
If it's cooked too much,

216
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:08,040
the meat gets tough. Right, Mr. Men?

217
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:13,440
Now I really believe
that you like the same things I do.

218
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:19,800
Excuse me.

219
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:25,080
What exactly
is the relationship between you two?

220
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:27,959
- We are--
- Cousins.

221
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:31,840
We're very close, like siblings.

222
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:36,919
That's a relief.

223
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,160
Alright.

224
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:44,240
Then please enjoy your dinner.

225
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:46,359
Excuse me.

226
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:48,840
Win. Win.

227
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:56,039
Please don't mind him.

228
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:58,840
He's always been protective of me,
like a little sister.

229
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:03,760
It's alright.
If I had a sister as beautiful as you,

230
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:06,520
I'd be protective too.

231
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:56,000
Here you are.
I've been looking everywhere for you.

232
00:22:57,040 --> 00:23:00,840
Why bother? If I die right now,

233
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:02,760
you probably wouldn't care.

234
00:23:05,560 --> 00:23:08,600
Win, you're sulking again.

235
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:11,560
I'm doing this for both of us.

236
00:23:12,240 --> 00:23:15,240
I have a plan.

237
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:18,360
What plan?

238
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:23,920
A plan to get Mr. Men to hand over
his money and treasures to us.

239
00:23:24,600 --> 00:23:27,919
Oh, Pat. You think I'm stupid?

240
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:31,719
We came here for the Black Coral
that's supposedly worth a fortune.

241
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:34,120
Why would we need Mr. Men's money?

242
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:36,199
Just admit it. You like him.

243
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:37,640
Are you crazy, Win?

244
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:41,639
We still don't know
where the Black Coral is.

245
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:45,080
We're just guessing.
We might never find it.

246
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:51,080
And how are you so sure Mr. Men is rich?

247
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:54,640
At first, I wasn't completely sure.

248
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:58,040
But earlier, while I was looking for you,

249
00:23:58,840 --> 00:24:00,120
I saw...

250
00:24:03,640 --> 00:24:04,840
Win.

251
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:46,360
Be careful. Pick them up.

252
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:48,440
Someone might see us.

253
00:25:04,120 --> 00:25:06,680
Pat, you weren't seeing things, were you?

254
00:25:08,280 --> 00:25:11,639
Win, I saw it clearly
with my own two eyes.

255
00:25:11,640 --> 00:25:13,560
Gold bars, Win.

256
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:17,640
Each crate must have at least 30 bars.

257
00:25:18,240 --> 00:25:21,920
There were dozens of crates.
I don't even know how much that's worth.

258
00:25:22,560 --> 00:25:26,160
Where did Mr. Men get that much gold from?

259
00:25:26,760 --> 00:25:28,759
Is he involved in some illegal business?

260
00:25:28,760 --> 00:25:32,799
Why should we care? What I care about
is how we're going to make

261
00:25:32,800 --> 00:25:34,360
all that gold ours.

262
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:38,880
Do you have a way?

263
00:25:39,960 --> 00:25:41,120
Of course.

264
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:44,799
You saw how interested

265
00:25:44,800 --> 00:25:47,159
Mr. Men is in me.

266
00:25:47,160 --> 00:25:50,880
All I have to do is please him.

267
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:55,840
The important thing is you.
Don't ruin this.

268
00:25:56,760 --> 00:25:59,559
Oh, Pat, I'm jealous of you.

269
00:25:59,560 --> 00:26:00,599
Ugh.

270
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:02,280
Don't be stupid.

271
00:26:02,960 --> 00:26:06,479
Trust me. We have to work together.

272
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:08,839
Once we get the gold, we leave.

273
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:13,359
We won't even have to tire ourselves out
diving for that Black Coral anymore. Deal?

274
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:14,680
Okay?

275
00:26:19,040 --> 00:26:22,160
Fine. I'm doing this for you.

276
00:26:23,960 --> 00:26:28,480
That's my darling.
We're going to be filthy rich.

277
00:26:44,600 --> 00:26:48,440
Greed will lead them to their deaths
without them even realizing it.

278
00:26:49,800 --> 00:26:51,600
Make them comfortable.

279
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:57,200
Do everything to put them at ease
until the night of the dark moon.

280
00:26:58,560 --> 00:27:02,080
I will use their corrupt blood
as an offering.

281
00:27:34,240 --> 00:27:36,360
You seem to like this boy very much.

282
00:27:39,840 --> 00:27:41,640
When I was a spirit,

283
00:27:42,840 --> 00:27:45,120
I met Kang several times.

284
00:27:48,920 --> 00:27:50,040
No wonder.

285
00:27:53,040 --> 00:27:54,800
The first time I saw him,

286
00:27:56,720 --> 00:27:58,720
he reminded me of our child.

287
00:28:01,360 --> 00:28:05,800
If he were still alive,
he would be about Kang's age.

288
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:09,640
That's true.

289
00:28:11,120 --> 00:28:14,639
I felt drawn to him from the first time
I met him at the fishpond house too.

290
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:16,160
I don't know why.

291
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:32,760
You must miss our child very much.

292
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:36,520
Yes.

293
00:28:41,040 --> 00:28:45,440
Don't worry.
I will find our child, no matter what.

294
00:28:51,600 --> 00:28:53,040
Mr. Phum,

295
00:28:54,560 --> 00:28:56,880
there's something I'd like to ask of you.

296
00:28:57,880 --> 00:29:01,080
Whatever you want,
I can give you anything.

297
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:12,640
Whether we find our child or not,

298
00:29:13,760 --> 00:29:17,240
I want you to take this boy in too.

299
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:20,040
You read my mind.

300
00:29:21,520 --> 00:29:23,999
I was just thinking I should
ask Venerable Sir Thongdee

301
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,800
if I could take Kang in.

302
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:32,800
Little boy,

303
00:29:34,880 --> 00:29:37,560
you won't have to be an orphan anymore.

304
00:29:45,560 --> 00:29:47,200
Mom.

305
00:29:48,120 --> 00:29:49,440
Dad.

306
00:29:53,240 --> 00:29:57,440
Mom. Dad.

307
00:30:23,680 --> 00:30:24,720
Pat.

308
00:30:26,760 --> 00:30:28,120
Pat, open the door.

309
00:30:30,480 --> 00:30:31,440
Pat.

310
00:30:38,400 --> 00:30:39,480
Pat.

311
00:30:42,240 --> 00:30:43,840
When did I fall asleep?

312
00:30:45,240 --> 00:30:46,080
Pat.

313
00:30:49,120 --> 00:30:50,000
Pat.

314
00:30:56,200 --> 00:30:57,320
Ugh.

315
00:31:04,920 --> 00:31:07,400
Pat, how did last night go?

316
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:15,480
It was a failure.

317
00:31:18,120 --> 00:31:19,239
Don't tell me

318
00:31:19,240 --> 00:31:22,800
Mr. Men didn't fall for your charm.

319
00:31:26,680 --> 00:31:30,079
Hey, Win. Don't insult me like that.

320
00:31:30,080 --> 00:31:31,719
I'm not that useless.

321
00:31:31,720 --> 00:31:34,440
Oh, Pat, you're the one who said

322
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:36,519
it was a failure.

323
00:31:36,520 --> 00:31:39,759
Well, after I left you,

324
00:31:39,760 --> 00:31:42,799
I came in to get dressed
and planned to go see Mr. Men.

325
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:45,079
But somehow,

326
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:48,960
I fell asleep. When I woke up,
I heard you knocking on the door.

327
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:54,039
Pat.

328
00:31:54,040 --> 00:31:55,079
Ugh.

329
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:57,039
Something feels very wrong.

330
00:31:57,040 --> 00:31:58,800
Last night I slept like the dead too.

331
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:02,120
And the last time I went to Skull Island,

332
00:32:02,880 --> 00:32:04,840
it didn't take this long to reach it.

333
00:32:06,040 --> 00:32:09,560
Hey, Pat, are we being tricked?

334
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:14,799
Oh, Win. What do we have
for Mr. Men to trick us out of?

335
00:32:14,800 --> 00:32:17,600
We're the ones who are going to trick him.

336
00:32:19,440 --> 00:32:21,959
Now get out.
I need to shower and get dressed.

337
00:32:21,960 --> 00:32:25,520
- Pat, but I think--
- Just get out.

338
00:32:26,560 --> 00:32:27,440
Go.

339
00:33:18,080 --> 00:33:20,080
Good Morning, Mr. Men.

340
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,200
Please.

341
00:33:24,080 --> 00:33:25,120
Thank you.

342
00:33:32,080 --> 00:33:33,240
Please have a seat.

343
00:33:34,600 --> 00:33:38,280
The atmosphere is very good here.

344
00:33:41,160 --> 00:33:44,320
Where exactly are we going?

345
00:33:46,120 --> 00:33:48,920
You wanted to go to Skull Island,
didn't you?

346
00:33:50,920 --> 00:33:55,240
Yes. But the Skull Island I went to before

347
00:33:55,840 --> 00:33:57,600
wasn't this far.

348
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:01,040
You're very clever.

349
00:34:03,280 --> 00:34:05,480
Does that mean
we're not really going to Skull Island?

350
00:34:06,680 --> 00:34:07,680
We are.

351
00:34:09,639 --> 00:34:13,239
But I want this trip to Skull Island

352
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:18,239
to be something very special.

353
00:34:19,120 --> 00:34:23,679
Something you will remember
until the day you die.

354
00:34:26,239 --> 00:34:30,079
When you speak so mysteriously,

355
00:34:30,080 --> 00:34:33,080
it only makes me more curious
about your surprise.

356
00:34:35,480 --> 00:34:37,239
You'll find out tonight.

357
00:34:38,760 --> 00:34:43,159
I can't wait.

358
00:35:02,240 --> 00:35:03,360
Thank you.

359
00:35:37,560 --> 00:35:40,720
This is the surprise
you were talking about for Pat?

360
00:35:41,760 --> 00:35:43,039
Yes.

361
00:35:43,040 --> 00:35:44,200
Whoa.

362
00:35:45,040 --> 00:35:46,960
It looks like some kind
of human sacrifice ritual.

363
00:35:48,040 --> 00:35:50,880
Win, why would you talk
to Mr. Men like that?

364
00:35:51,520 --> 00:35:54,800
Can't you see this, Pat?
I think we should leave.

365
00:35:55,640 --> 00:35:58,160
There's definitely
something suspicious going on here.

366
00:35:58,800 --> 00:36:01,679
Hey, if you don't know what you're
talking about, then stay quiet.

367
00:36:01,680 --> 00:36:04,280
Pat, have you gone crazy?

368
00:36:05,360 --> 00:36:09,559
Mr. Men already told me. The theme
is supposed to be scary and exciting.

369
00:36:09,560 --> 00:36:11,559
It excites us.

370
00:36:11,560 --> 00:36:13,840
Why would anyone throw a party like this?

371
00:36:15,720 --> 00:36:17,920
Because tonight
is the night of the new moon.

372
00:36:20,080 --> 00:36:21,560
The night of the new moon?

373
00:36:22,160 --> 00:36:23,440
A lunar eclipse, Win.

374
00:36:24,680 --> 00:36:25,880
How do you know that?

375
00:36:27,120 --> 00:36:31,640
Mr. Men told me everything.
Will you stop complaining already?

376
00:36:35,040 --> 00:36:39,480
Ms. Pat, you should go get changed.
My men have prepared everything for you.

377
00:36:41,520 --> 00:36:43,480
Yes. Thank you.

378
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:45,920
This way, please.

379
00:37:11,520 --> 00:37:12,560
Please.

380
00:37:13,600 --> 00:37:14,680
Thank you.

381
00:37:25,120 --> 00:37:26,959
Win,

382
00:37:26,960 --> 00:37:30,520
can you stop saying
and doing things that annoy Mr. Men?

383
00:37:32,040 --> 00:37:32,919
Pat,

384
00:37:32,920 --> 00:37:36,879
no matter what, I still think
this is weird. No one does this.

385
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:38,760
I think Mr. Men
is some kind of psychopath.

386
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:42,199
Stop imagining things.

387
00:37:42,200 --> 00:37:45,280
Everyone has different tastes.

388
00:38:18,160 --> 00:38:21,159
Win, come look at this.

389
00:38:21,160 --> 00:38:25,120
These pieces are all real.

390
00:38:31,880 --> 00:38:32,720
Wait, Pat.

391
00:38:33,920 --> 00:38:36,280
How do you know they're real?

392
00:38:36,920 --> 00:38:41,000
I'm a woman. I know jewelry when I see it.

393
00:38:42,240 --> 00:38:44,360
Even for a costume party,

394
00:38:44,960 --> 00:38:47,000
he uses real jewelry.

395
00:38:47,520 --> 00:38:51,240
He must be unbelievably rich.

396
00:38:53,240 --> 00:38:55,680
How am I this lucky?

397
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:17,280
It's so beautiful.

398
00:40:07,800 --> 00:40:09,240
Mr. Men.

399
00:40:19,560 --> 00:40:21,680
You're so beautiful, Ms. Pat.

400
00:40:27,080 --> 00:40:29,440
- Please.
- Thank you.

401
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:48,680
If it weren't for the gold,

402
00:40:49,600 --> 00:40:50,920
I wouldn't stay here for a second.

403
00:41:27,880 --> 00:41:29,120
This feels better.

404
00:42:14,280 --> 00:42:16,280
Ghosts! Ghosts!

405
00:42:40,560 --> 00:42:42,280
Mr. Men.

406
00:42:43,800 --> 00:42:45,440
These corpses

407
00:42:47,080 --> 00:42:49,040
look so real.

408
00:42:52,520 --> 00:42:55,040
I thought you'd be frightened.

409
00:42:55,680 --> 00:42:58,280
Most people would think I'm strange.

410
00:43:00,560 --> 00:43:04,439
Not at all. I like strange things.

411
00:43:04,440 --> 00:43:08,320
It's thrilling. Exciting.

412
00:43:18,200 --> 00:43:19,920
Where did Win go?

413
00:43:25,240 --> 00:43:26,719
Mr. Men,

414
00:43:26,720 --> 00:43:30,039
if Win said anything offensive,

415
00:43:30,040 --> 00:43:31,839
please don't take it personally.

416
00:43:31,840 --> 00:43:35,920
He's just a blunt person.
Deep down, he doesn't mean anything by it.

417
00:43:37,600 --> 00:43:38,520
Of course.

418
00:43:57,240 --> 00:44:01,239
Pat. Pat. Pat.

419
00:44:01,240 --> 00:44:05,159
Let's get out of here.
There are ghosts all over the island.

420
00:44:05,160 --> 00:44:06,600
Let's run, Pat. Look!

421
00:44:09,320 --> 00:44:10,680
Pat, look!

422
00:44:13,640 --> 00:44:14,960
Let's run, Pat!

423
00:44:23,000 --> 00:44:26,639
No. Don't! I'm scared!

424
00:44:26,640 --> 00:44:28,359
No!

425
00:44:28,360 --> 00:44:29,719
Don't.

426
00:44:29,720 --> 00:44:31,320
What is this in the drawing?

427
00:44:32,800 --> 00:44:35,160
Could it be Sairung, Mr. Phum's wife?

428
00:44:36,440 --> 00:44:39,600
If you come any closer, I'll shoot you.

429
00:44:41,760 --> 00:44:42,880
Kaimook!

430
00:45:17,520 --> 00:45:19,320
Subtitle translation by: Panuwat Baikeawon
